
  <sn><md>### Soil and Enviromental Chemistry

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-md-6
The scope of soil and environmental chemistry centers on understanding the `chemical composition, reactions, and processes` that govern the behavior of `substances within soil` and `at its interfaces` with water, air, and living organisms. 
It is an `interdisciplinary field` that combines principles of `chemistry, geology, and biology` to study both `natural soil systems` and the `fate of contaminants` introduced by human activity.
:::

